The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/core/core-11-autosizing.md`.

**Key findings summary:**

- **3 High**: (1) Single algebraic solve instead of iterative design-day simulation — misses thermal mass lag and diurnal peak timing; (2) No internal gains in cooling sizing — potential undersizing; (3) No water heater autosizing methodology at all.
- **1 Medium**: Cooling sizing at solar noon only misses west-facing window peaks.
- **2 Low**: Oversizing factors and limits correctly implemented (positive); heating sizing correctly ignores solar/internal gains (positive).

The fundamental architectural difference from EnergyPlus is that HARES uses a one-shot `solve_for_output_input` algebraic solve rather than running actual design-day simulations with ideal loads systems across a 24-hour weather profile.
